	<h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
	<p class="page-lede">Energy & geopolitics expert, lecturer and columnist.</p>
	<div class="page-body">
<p>Romain Blachier analyses energy and geopolitics, with a focus on Taiwan and the Indo-Pacific (energy security, semiconductors, China-Taiwan relations).</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>18 years</strong> in the energy sector at Compagnie Nationale du Rhône (France's 3rd-largest electricity producer).</li>
<li><strong>12 years</strong> as an elected official in the Lyon metropolitan area (culture, digital, international).</li>
<li>Lecturer since 2010: Sciences Po Paris, Grenoble École de Management, IEP Lyon, Université Lyon 1, ILERI, HEIP.</li>
<li>President of the France-Formosa Association.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Expertise</h2>
<p>Energy markets and geopolitics, energy transition and sovereignty, Taiwan &amp; Indo-Pacific, comparative political systems, strategic and crisis communications, public affairs.</p>
<h2>Languages</h2>
<p>French, English, Mandarin.</p>
